	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "OPSCO Optoelectronics SK6805-EC15, single-wire addressable RGB LED, SMD-4P 1.5x1.5x0.65mm (LCSC C2890035, docs/sourcing.md). Datasheet: iPixel LED SK6805-EC15 REV.04 EN-20190527 (lcsc.com/datasheet/lcsc_datasheet_2412101523_OPSCO-Optoelectronics-SK6805-EC15_C2890035.pdf). Pin table (matches sierra-to-usb:SK6805-EC15 symbol exactly): 1=DIN, 2=VDD, 3=DOUT, 4=GND. Real stock KiCad match found under a DIFFERENT chip name -- LED_SMD.pretty/LED_SK6812_EC15_1.5x1.5mm.kicad_mod -- is the SAME physical 'EC15' 1.5x1.5mm 4-pad commodity mini-LED package family (SK6805-EC15 and SK6812-EC15 are pin/pad-compatible sibling chips in this industry-standard package, both marketed as WS2812-mini-class parts); that stock file's own description notes 'orientation mark at GND', and its chamfered corner sits at the pad-4 (bottom-left) position, consistent with this project's pin4=GND assignment. Pad geometry (0.5x0.5mm roundrect pads at +/-0.45mm, 1.5x1.5mm body, chamfered GND corner) is copied directly from that real stock file rather than re-derived, since it is dimensionally verified stock KiCad data for this exact package family. The OTHER stock candidate, LED_SMD.pretty/LED_SK6805_PLCC4_2.4x2.7mm_P1.3mm.kicad_mod, was rejected per task instructions as the wrong physical size (2.4x2.7mm vs actual 1.5x1.5mm). Not used directly under its own SK6812 name because Value/Datasheet/Description must correctly identify the SK6805-EC15 part actually populated at U28.")
	(tags "LED RGB NeoPixel SK6805 SK6805-EC15 addressable single-wire")
